  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nWe propose an adaptive spectral annealing algorithm that leverages the Fourier transform properties to search for a step function with minimal maximum overlap. Our core idea is to separate the optimization into two phases: (1) Global exploration using simulated annealing with thresholded frequency components to escape local optima, and (2) Local refinement with constrained gradient projection. The spectral decomposition allows us to systematically suppress high-magnitude frequency components associated with large correlation peaks. The algorithm dynamically adjusts its search intensity based on spectral observations, prioritizing regions that yield better overlap reduction.\n\nMathematical specification:\n1. Represent step function h:[0,2] \u2192 [0,1] with n-point grid\n2. Objective: min max\u2096 [\u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx] dx\n3. Constraints: 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 for all i, \u2211h[i] = n/2\n4. Optimization formulation:\n   - Variables: h \u2208 [0,1]^n\n   - Objective: exp(-\u03b2(max\u2096 ((h \u2217 (1-h))[k] * dx - M)))\n   - Constraints: \u2211h[i] = n/2, 0\u2264h[i]\u22641\n\nImplementation procedure:\n\n1. Initialization:\n   - Start with initial_h_values (if provided)\n   - Clip and normalize to [0,1] with sum n/2\n   - Set dx = 2.0/n, L=nearest power of 2 \u2265 (2n-1)\n\n2. Spectral analysis:\n   def spectrale_analysis(h):\n      fh = np.fft.rfft(h, L)\n      psd = np.abs(fh)**2 / n  # Power spectral density\n      return psd, np.argmax(psd)  # Get peak frequency\n\n3. Simulated annealing phase:\n   def adaptive_annealing(h, current_val, temp_scale=0.8):\n      # Calculate correlations\n      corr = correlate_full(h)\n      max_corr = corr.max() * dx\n      \n      # Identify high-magnitude frequencies\n      psd, peak_index = spectrale_analysis(np.real(np.fft.irfft(np.fft.rfft(h, L)[: (L//2)]) )\n      damp_factor = 0.3 if psd[peak_index] > 1.5 else 0.1\n      \n      # Generate neighbor with spectral perturbation\n      pert_factor = min(1.0, (1.0/max_corr * n)**0.2)\n      new_h = h.copy()\n      rand_idx = rng.choice(n, min(10, int(n*pert_factor)))\n      new_h[rand_idx] += (rng.random()-0.5)*damp_factor*0.2\n      new_h = np.clip(new_h, 0,1)\n      new_h = enforce_sum(new_h, n/2, rng)\n      \n      # Check improvement\n      new_corr = compute_c5(new_h)\n      if new_corr < current_val or rng.random() < min(0.7, temp_scale):\n          return new_h, new_corr\n      return h, max_corr\n\n4. Local refinement:\n   def gradient_repair(h, target_sum, lr=0.1):\n      # Project gradient (2nd derivative prior)\n      conv2 = correlate_full((1-h)[::-1])[:n-1]\n      dz = np.gradient(conv2, dx)\n      dg = conv2 / (np.std(conv2)**2)  # Information gain\n      grad = (target_sum - h.sum())  # Constraint violation\n\n      # Apply gradient projection\n      for _ in range(50):\n          for i in range(n):\n              max_change = min(lr, min(1-h[i], h[i])/np.abs(dz[i]))\n              h[i] = np.clip(h[i] + 0.1*max_change*dg[i], 0,1)\n          h = enforce_sum(h, n/2, rng)\n      return h\n\n5. Main optimization loop:\n   budget = budget_s * 0.8\n   start_time = time.time()\n   h = initial_h_values.copy() if 'initial_h_values' in globals() else random_feasible_vector(n, rng)\n   h = np.clip(h, 0,1); h = enforce_sum(h, n/2, rng)\n   current_value = compute_c5(h)\n   best_h, best_value = h.copy(), current_value\n\n   while time.time() < start_time + budget:\n      h, new_value = adaptive_annealing(h, current_value)\n      current_value = new_value\n      if current_value < best_value:\n          best_h, best_value = h.copy(), current_value\n      \n      # Local refinement\n      if rng.random() < 0.3:\n          h = gradient_repair(h, n/2, lr=0.05)\n          current_value = compute_c5(h)\n          if current_value < best_value: update best\n\n      # Temperature schedule\n      if time.time() - start_time < budget * 0.4 and rng.random() < 0.05:\n          h = random_feasible_vector(n, rng)\n          h = enforce_sum(h, n/2, rng)\n          current_value = compute_c5(h)\n\n   # Upsampling if budget permits\n   remaining_budget = budget_s - (time.time() - start_time)\n   if n < 400 and remaining_budget > 30:\n      n_up = n * 2\n      h_up = np.repeat(best_h, 2)\n      h_up = enforce_sum(h_up, n_up/2, rng)\n      # Apply local search on upsampled grid...\n\n   return best_h.tolist(), float(best_value), n\n\nSearch choices and useful variations:\n- Use pure frequency damping for large deviations\n- Recursive variance-based normalization of gradient descent\n- Temperature scaling based on global spectral entropy\n- Multi-resolution analysis for adaptive grid\n- Introduce periodicity-based constraints for phase matching\n\nCompute budget and robustness:\n- Initial: 80% budget for main search\n- Falls back to random restarts if stuck\n- Graceful degradation:\n  - clip_to_bounds(h) = np.clip(h,0,1)\n  - repair_sum(h) = enforce_sum(h, n/2, rng)\n  - handle NaN/Inf: return safe_candidate\n\nValidation and return contract:\n1. Check: sum(best_h) == n/2 within tolerance\n2. Check boundaries: all(0 <= h <= 1)\n3. Compute candidate score: compute_c5(best_h)\n4. Error handling: return fallback solution if:\n   - Initial solution is infeasible\n   - Optimization exceeds budget\n   - Results display convergence pattern\n   - Values are NaN or exceed bounds\n\nKey parameters:\n- READ_TEMPERATURE = 0.85 (temperature decay)\n- DAMPING_FACTOR = 0.35 (frequency threshold multiplier)\n- CONVERGENCE_THRESHOLD = 1e-6 (improvement limit)",
